  "about": "What each pin's incident_start stands for. Kept apart from the hand-checked pin files so those files, their fingerprints and the owner approvals stay untouched. Every active pin needs an entry here or tools/publish.py stops. See tools/incident_dates.py for the format.",
  "bases": {
    "incident": "incident_start is when it happened or began; with incident_event 'found', when a body or a fault was found.",
    "report": "The sources never say when it happened, so incident_start is the report or notice date. The incident date is unknown and charts count it as date not stated.",
    "later_step": "incident_start is a later step (arrest, charge, court appearance or finding) in an older case. The incident itself is on earlier_incident.date, quoted in evidence. Charts do not put it on the day of the later step."
  },
